1
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:04,546
PARK MINJAE'S LIST

2
00:00:04,630 --> 00:00:05,923
START DATING...

3
00:00:36,620 --> 00:00:40,958
BETWEEN STEPS

4
00:00:41,583 --> 00:00:43,835
CHARACTERS, PLACES, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND EVENTS IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

5
00:00:43,919 --> 00:00:45,546
THIS DRAMA CONTAINS SENSITIVE CONTENT

6
00:02:01,121 --> 00:02:02,122
EPISODE 3

7
00:02:03,832 --> 00:02:04,833
You're late.

8
00:02:05,625 --> 00:02:09,171
Yeah, I haven't seen these friends
in a while, and I lost track of time.

9
00:02:09,254 --> 00:02:10,839
You didn't drink much, did you?

10
00:02:10,922 --> 00:02:14,176
No, not much. Just a little with dinner.

11
00:02:15,677 --> 00:02:16,887
Don't lock the door yet.

12
00:02:17,471 --> 00:02:18,889
Youjin is not home.

13
00:02:20,515 --> 00:02:22,225
She's still not home at this hour?

14
00:02:23,977 --> 00:02:26,438
The other grad students
threw her a welcome party.

15
00:02:27,105 --> 00:02:28,106
Oh.

16
00:02:42,954 --> 00:02:44,039
Jeez, you scared me.

17
00:02:44,623 --> 00:02:45,957
What are you doing?

18
00:02:46,541 --> 00:02:48,251
-Honey.
-Let go.

19
00:02:48,335 --> 00:02:52,923
So I was on my way home just now,
and you know that alley next to our place?

20
00:02:53,423 --> 00:02:55,926
There's a streetlight there, right?

21
00:02:56,009 --> 00:02:57,010
A streetlight?

22
00:02:57,511 --> 00:02:58,637
Yeah.

23
00:02:58,720 --> 00:03:03,725
There were these two young people there,
holding each other and kissing.

24
00:03:04,851 --> 00:03:06,895
-In the alley right next to our place?
-Yeah.

25
00:03:06,978 --> 00:03:08,438
Oh my. Who were they?

26
00:03:08,522 --> 00:03:10,440
Do you know them?
Do they live around here?

27
00:03:11,400 --> 00:03:14,194
I don't know. I've never seen them before.

28
00:03:15,237 --> 00:03:20,409
But seeing them reminded me of us
back when we were dating, you know?

29
00:03:20,492 --> 00:03:21,493
What?

30
00:03:23,161 --> 00:03:25,956
How about a kiss? It's been a while.

31
00:03:26,039 --> 00:03:28,708
Stop it. What's gotten into you?

32
00:03:28,792 --> 00:03:30,460
Come on. Just one kiss.

33
00:03:30,544 --> 00:03:32,587
God, stop it.

34
00:03:33,213 --> 00:03:35,966
Miyoung, come on. Just give me one kiss.

35
00:03:36,049 --> 00:03:38,802
Come on, I said no. Stop it!

36
00:03:38,885 --> 00:03:40,554
Please, just one kiss.

37
00:03:40,637 --> 00:03:43,223
Stop it. Gosh, stop. [giggling]

38
00:03:43,306 --> 00:03:45,517
Jeez, will you guys stop already?

39
00:03:46,935 --> 00:03:48,103
Dad, are you drunk?

40
00:03:49,354 --> 00:03:52,941
If you're drunk, just go to bed.
Stop bothering Mom and leave her alone.

41
00:03:53,567 --> 00:03:55,026
Come on, go to bed already.

42
00:03:55,110 --> 00:03:57,112
-[digital beep from door]
-What are you doing? Come on.

43
00:03:57,195 --> 00:03:59,281
-[Youjin] I'm home.
-[door closes]

44
00:04:01,199 --> 00:04:02,701
You need to come home earlier.

45
00:04:02,784 --> 00:04:03,785
-Hey!
-[Youjin] Okay.

46
00:04:03,869 --> 00:04:05,787
Do you know what time it is?

47
00:04:06,329 --> 00:04:08,623
You need to start
coming home earlier, young lady.

48
00:04:08,707 --> 00:04:11,042
Look at the time!
You've been drinking, haven't you?

49
00:04:11,543 --> 00:04:14,337
Hey. Don't call your sister
"young lady," okay?

50
00:04:14,421 --> 00:04:16,506
And what do you mean,
your dad is bothering me?

51
00:04:16,590 --> 00:04:20,177
You're the one who bothers me the most,
you know? It's you. God!

52
00:05:12,521 --> 00:05:13,772
I don't know.

53
00:06:10,078 --> 00:06:13,290
SLAM DUNK

54
00:06:59,294 --> 00:07:03,632
SEOHAN NATIONAL UNIVERSITY TEST PAPER
NAME LIM YOUJIN

55
00:07:08,970 --> 00:07:11,097
TEST PAPER
NAME KIM SEJIN

56
00:07:12,682 --> 00:07:14,684
-[door opens]

57
00:07:59,354 --> 00:08:01,356
No matter how much you do it, we...

58
00:08:01,439 --> 00:08:03,692
-You're already here.
-Hello.

59
00:08:03,775 --> 00:08:05,985
Youjin, you're here early.

60
00:08:06,069 --> 00:08:07,612
She got here earlier than we did.

61
00:08:07,696 --> 00:08:09,614
[Youjin] I can't be late on the first day.

62
00:08:10,240 --> 00:08:13,118
You never disappoint, Youjin.
That's why I got you a coffee.

63
00:08:13,201 --> 00:08:15,203
Thank you. I appreciate it.

64
00:08:18,873 --> 00:08:19,958
Who are you?

65
00:08:28,550 --> 00:08:30,135
[Taeho] <i>Minjae, where are you?</i>

66
00:08:31,136 --> 00:08:33,763
[Minjae] <i>On the bus.</i>
<i>I'll be there in five.</i>

67
00:08:40,270 --> 00:08:42,480
<i>Did Youjin come?</i>

68
00:08:49,821 --> 00:08:51,072
<i>What about Lim Youjin?</i>

69
00:08:58,288 --> 00:08:59,956
<i>Did our new lab mate Youjin...</i>

70
00:09:07,047 --> 00:09:09,549
Morning. Morning.

71
00:09:10,383 --> 00:09:12,552
[in English] Morning. Good morning.

72
00:09:13,386 --> 00:09:14,596
Good morning.

73
00:09:16,473 --> 00:09:17,557
[in Korean] Morning.

74
00:09:17,640 --> 00:09:20,060
I'm Kim Sejin. Nice to meet you.

75
00:09:20,769 --> 00:09:21,770
All right.

76
00:09:24,606 --> 00:09:25,607
Okay, sit down.

77
00:09:26,566 --> 00:09:30,862
I thought Sejin wouldn't be joining us
until the semester started,

78
00:09:30,945 --> 00:09:33,990
but he said he could start this month,
so I had him come in early.

79
00:09:35,575 --> 00:09:39,287
He's new to our school, so help him
settle in and look out for him.

80
00:09:39,913 --> 00:09:40,914
Oh, okay.

81
00:09:43,792 --> 00:09:44,793
Yes.

82
00:09:45,752 --> 00:09:49,506
I thought you said
there was only one opening in the lab,

83
00:09:50,840 --> 00:09:52,050
but there are two of us.

84
00:09:52,884 --> 00:09:53,885
Right.

85
00:09:54,761 --> 00:10:00,350
We... Our school might be competing
in the WRS this year,

86
00:10:01,643 --> 00:10:04,521
so the professor told me
to take on one more student.

87
00:10:04,604 --> 00:10:07,065
[whispering] Hey, what's the WRS?

88
00:10:07,148 --> 00:10:09,234
[whispering] It's the World Robot Summit.

89
00:10:10,193 --> 00:10:11,194
Yes?

90
00:10:11,736 --> 00:10:14,322
But she doesn't even know what the WRS is.

91
00:10:14,405 --> 00:10:17,742
Lim Youjin is a student
from another department,

92
00:10:17,826 --> 00:10:19,494
so she'll still have a lot to learn.

93
00:10:19,577 --> 00:10:22,247
So I'd like you to look out for her
and help her settle in.

94
00:10:23,498 --> 00:10:25,625
-What is it?
-Then do we get paid the same?

95
00:10:26,751 --> 00:10:28,837
-Yes, you'll get paid the same.
-Wait, but--

96
00:10:28,920 --> 00:10:33,341
Let's get you two set up with desks first.
Let's see. Get up.

97
00:10:33,424 --> 00:10:34,425
Then...

98
00:10:41,141 --> 00:10:42,142
Ah.

99
00:10:42,225 --> 00:10:45,228
Youjin, you take this desk.
And Sejin, you take this one.

100
00:10:48,731 --> 00:10:51,693
But there's no computer at my desk.
There's nothing here.

101
00:10:52,735 --> 00:10:55,822
I ordered a computer.
It should be here soon.

102
00:10:56,739 --> 00:10:58,783
So until then...

103
00:10:58,867 --> 00:11:02,078
You brought your own laptop, right?
Just use that for now.

104
00:11:02,829 --> 00:11:04,289
I only brought my tablet.

105
00:11:05,874 --> 00:11:07,125
You can use that for now.

106
00:11:36,070 --> 00:11:37,697
-Minjae?
-Yes.

107
00:11:37,780 --> 00:11:40,283
I think this computer is lagging.

108
00:11:41,618 --> 00:11:44,370
Right. It's not lagging.

109
00:11:44,454 --> 00:11:46,998
That one's just a little slow
because it's old.

110
00:11:48,124 --> 00:11:49,751
-Yeah.
-Okay.

111
00:12:02,055 --> 00:12:04,224
So when will my computer get here?

112
00:12:04,307 --> 00:12:05,475
Uh...

113
00:12:05,558 --> 00:12:07,018
I'm not sure.

114
00:12:08,102 --> 00:12:10,897
They said it'd get here soon,
so just wait a bit.

115
00:12:12,899 --> 00:12:15,109
Then, until mine gets here,
how about this?

116
00:12:16,527 --> 00:12:21,366
What if we switch desks every day?
So we can take turns using the computer?

117
00:12:22,575 --> 00:12:25,954
Why should we take turns
using my computer? It's mine.

118
00:12:26,871 --> 00:12:29,749
How is this yours? It belongs to the lab.

119
00:12:31,251 --> 00:12:35,088
That's not what I mean.
The lab lead assigned it to me.

120
00:12:35,171 --> 00:12:36,631
[Hangyeol] Well...

121
00:12:38,049 --> 00:12:41,261
Why don't you play rock-paper-scissors
or ghost leg?

122
00:12:41,344 --> 00:12:43,930
The winner gets the computer.

123
00:12:44,013 --> 00:12:45,431
Yeah, that's a good idea.

124
00:12:46,015 --> 00:12:48,309
The winner gets the computer.
Fair and square.

125
00:12:48,393 --> 00:12:51,729
Come on, there's no need for ghost leg.

126
00:12:51,813 --> 00:12:53,314
We have to respect seniority.

127
00:12:53,898 --> 00:12:58,152
Youjin joined the lab three days earlier,
so she should get it.

128
00:12:58,236 --> 00:13:01,489
She has seniority over me just because
she joined three days earlier?

129
00:13:01,572 --> 00:13:02,573
That's ridiculous.

130
00:13:04,575 --> 00:13:09,706
Whether it's three days or three hours,
we take seniority seriously in this lab...

131
00:13:10,790 --> 00:13:11,833
Mr. Kim.

132
00:13:15,295 --> 00:13:17,714
Isn't this mine?

133
00:13:17,797 --> 00:13:19,299
It's yours.

134
00:13:20,800 --> 00:13:23,594
I mean, even if
you had a computer, Youjin,

135
00:13:23,678 --> 00:13:26,597
you don't have any actual work to do yet.

136
00:13:27,390 --> 00:13:31,686
So you can check your email
and look up papers

137
00:13:31,769 --> 00:13:33,646
on your, laptop...

138
00:13:33,730 --> 00:13:36,107
I mean, that tablet you brought for now.

139
00:13:36,607 --> 00:13:38,359
And your computer should be here soon.

140
00:13:38,943 --> 00:13:42,864
So just, yeah... Just wait a little bit.

141
00:14:10,600 --> 00:14:13,519
[Minjae] <i>I checked, and it looks like</i>
<i>the computer should be here soon.</i>

142
00:14:13,603 --> 00:14:15,438
<i>I think you won't have to wait long.</i>

143
00:14:20,818 --> 00:14:21,819
[Youjin] <i>Okay.</i>

144
00:14:37,794 --> 00:14:39,170
[Minjae] <i>Do you want some ice cream?</i>

145
00:14:40,213 --> 00:14:41,631
<i>What flavor do you like?</i>

146
00:14:50,431 --> 00:14:52,266
[Youjin] <i>I don't like ice cream.</i>

147
00:14:53,309 --> 00:14:55,353
<i>I absolutely hate it. I don't want any.</i>

148
00:14:56,395 --> 00:14:58,773
<i>And I will never eat it, ever.</i>
<i>It pisses me off.</i>

149
00:14:58,856 --> 00:15:00,775
<i>I hate it more than anything in the world.</i>

150
00:15:12,370 --> 00:15:14,247
[Hangyeol] Youjin, over here. No!

151
00:15:14,330 --> 00:15:15,331
[Taeho] Block her!

152
00:15:16,165 --> 00:15:17,166
Miss!

153
00:15:17,250 --> 00:15:18,251
-[grunts]
-[Youjin laughs]

154
00:15:18,334 --> 00:15:19,335
Nice!

155
00:15:19,919 --> 00:15:21,629
-[Sejin sighs]
-[chuckles softly]

156
00:15:21,712 --> 00:15:25,007
They suck at basketball.
They haven't made a single basket.

157
00:15:27,135 --> 00:15:28,136
[Chansoo] Hey, now...

158
00:15:28,219 --> 00:15:29,220
[Taeho] She can't make it.

159
00:15:29,637 --> 00:15:31,347
-[exclaims]
-[cheering]

160
00:15:33,015 --> 00:15:35,059
She's not even that pretty.

161
00:15:35,143 --> 00:15:37,311
What?

162
00:15:38,604 --> 00:15:41,774
Let's be honest. She only stands out
in an engineering school.

163
00:15:43,109 --> 00:15:45,153
There are plenty of pretty girls
at Hongik University.

164
00:15:45,236 --> 00:15:46,612
She's just average.

165
00:15:50,741 --> 00:15:52,368
Have you been to Hongik University?

166
00:15:55,621 --> 00:15:57,373
No, I haven't.

167
00:16:01,043 --> 00:16:02,044
I have.

168
00:16:03,212 --> 00:16:04,213
But...

169
00:16:06,549 --> 00:16:07,842
Well, I didn't see any...

170
00:16:08,426 --> 00:16:09,427
Let's go.

171
00:16:10,469 --> 00:16:11,637
Let's go. [sighs]

172
00:16:14,348 --> 00:16:18,227
Hey, you guys are no different.
Daejeon is a boring city. Why--

173
00:16:18,311 --> 00:16:20,521
That's not true.
Daejeon is a super fun city.

174
00:16:20,605 --> 00:16:22,732
"Super fun?"
Why are you getting all defensive?

175
00:16:22,815 --> 00:16:24,525
-[Sejin] No, seriously.
-What do you do there?

176
00:16:24,609 --> 00:16:25,735
[Sejin] A lot of things.

177
00:16:38,456 --> 00:16:39,457
Should I take it?

178
00:16:39,540 --> 00:16:42,293
Yeah. You can answer all the calls
from now on.

179
00:16:47,381 --> 00:16:49,467
This is Professor Ahn's lab.

180
00:16:50,676 --> 00:16:51,677
Yes.

181
00:16:52,637 --> 00:16:53,638
Yes.

182
00:16:56,265 --> 00:16:57,642
All right, got it.

183
00:17:03,272 --> 00:17:05,816
Professor Ahn's back from his appointment.

184
00:17:06,567 --> 00:17:07,652
Yeah?

185
00:17:08,152 --> 00:17:11,113
[Jaehong] You two are the same age
and in the same cohort,

186
00:17:11,197 --> 00:17:14,033
so just support each other
and get along, okay?

187
00:17:14,617 --> 00:17:17,245
"Loving your cohort
is loving your country."

188
00:17:17,328 --> 00:17:18,913
There's a saying like that.

189
00:17:18,996 --> 00:17:19,997
Right.

190
00:17:20,539 --> 00:17:22,625
[Jaehong] Sejin, did you find
a place to stay in Seoul?

191
00:17:23,501 --> 00:17:25,378
Yes. I found a place near campus.

192
00:17:25,962 --> 00:17:28,923
Actually, it's right by my place.

193
00:17:29,006 --> 00:17:31,300
Oh, that's great.
So you can help him out then.

194
00:17:32,552 --> 00:17:33,553
Sure.

195
00:17:33,636 --> 00:17:37,390
Anyway, I'm glad
Sejin was able to start early.

196
00:17:38,391 --> 00:17:41,227
And I hear KAIST is competing
in the WRS this year too?

197
00:17:41,811 --> 00:17:45,690
Yes. From what I've heard,
Professor Hwang Semin's lab will compete.

198
00:17:45,773 --> 00:17:48,943
But their funding from
the Ministry of National Defense was cut,

199
00:17:49,026 --> 00:17:51,445
so they sat out the last two years.

200
00:17:51,529 --> 00:17:53,197
What funding do they have this time?

201
00:17:53,739 --> 00:17:54,740
Uh...

202
00:17:55,741 --> 00:17:57,785
Not through
the Ministry of National Defense.

203
00:17:57,868 --> 00:18:00,288
KEIT plans to issue a call
for proposals this year.

204
00:18:00,371 --> 00:18:02,331
-That's probably why--
-KEIT?

205
00:18:05,126 --> 00:18:08,379
But I met Professor Hwang
at the seminar two weeks ago,

206
00:18:08,921 --> 00:18:10,381
and he didn't mention anything.

207
00:18:11,841 --> 00:18:13,718
Well, it's not official yet.

208
00:18:15,011 --> 00:18:19,599
But I heard 200 million won
has been earmarked for it.

209
00:18:19,682 --> 00:18:20,683
200 million?

210
00:18:22,184 --> 00:18:25,938
Wow. Hwang Semin, that sly fox.

211
00:18:26,022 --> 00:18:27,607
-Professor.
-Okay, fine.

212
00:18:28,566 --> 00:18:32,445
But where did you hear about it?
None of us knew about that.

213
00:18:32,528 --> 00:18:34,113
I heard it in the restroom.

214
00:18:35,281 --> 00:18:36,324
Restroom?

215
00:18:36,824 --> 00:18:38,242
While I was relieving myself.

216
00:18:39,952 --> 00:18:41,579
Well, I wasn't trying to listen in.

217
00:18:41,662 --> 00:18:44,290
I just happened to overhear him
talking on the phone.

218
00:18:44,373 --> 00:18:47,376
He's pretty sharp.

219
00:18:48,169 --> 00:18:49,170
Hmm.

220
00:18:50,338 --> 00:18:53,633
Anyway, we need to hurry up
and put together our own proposal.

221
00:18:53,716 --> 00:18:55,843
Okay, I'll make sure we're well prepared.

222
00:18:57,053 --> 00:18:58,721
Right.

223
00:18:58,804 --> 00:19:02,975
Didn't KEIT's RFP template
change last year?

224
00:19:03,601 --> 00:19:05,311
Yes, I'll check.

225
00:19:05,394 --> 00:19:07,563
Okay, please look into that first.

226
00:19:07,647 --> 00:19:10,191
And keep an eye out.
We don't know when it'll be posted.

227
00:19:10,274 --> 00:19:11,609
-Okay.
-All right.

228
00:19:11,692 --> 00:19:13,235
What is KEIT?

229
00:19:13,903 --> 00:19:17,073
Korea Planning and Evaluation Institute
of Industrial Technology, Ms. Lim.

230
00:19:17,156 --> 00:19:18,157
It's an acronym.

231
00:19:19,700 --> 00:19:21,369
That little rat...

232
00:19:22,161 --> 00:19:23,663
[Chansoo] Why is KEIT doing

233
00:19:23,746 --> 00:19:25,915
what the Ministry of National Defense
used to do?

234
00:19:26,499 --> 00:19:29,752
The civilian sector can be dangerous too,
like industrial accident sites.

235
00:19:29,835 --> 00:19:31,462
So I guess they'd be interested.

236
00:19:31,545 --> 00:19:35,883
So we need to have everything in place
to reach around TRL 7 or 8,

237
00:19:35,966 --> 00:19:39,679
or at least TRL 5 or 6, to the point
where it's ready for application.

238
00:19:41,681 --> 00:19:43,891
Both the robot design
and the control technology

239
00:19:43,974 --> 00:19:45,601
are our proprietary technologies.

240
00:19:45,685 --> 00:19:47,812
Make sure to emphasize
that all key components,

241
00:19:47,895 --> 00:19:50,189
like the actuators and encoders,
are made in Korea.

242
00:19:50,272 --> 00:19:51,691
-Okay, got it.
-Good.

243
00:19:52,650 --> 00:19:55,069
We'll need to include
the simulation results too.

244
00:19:55,152 --> 00:19:58,572
And of course, we'll need visuals
to highlight all of that, right?

245
00:20:00,324 --> 00:20:02,910
We just need something rough now.
We can revise it later.

246
00:20:03,577 --> 00:20:07,206
What matters is having a preliminary draft
ready by the end of the month.

247
00:20:07,289 --> 00:20:08,499
So let's get moving.

248
00:20:09,458 --> 00:20:10,459
Okay.

249
00:20:13,379 --> 00:20:15,131
-[Chansoo] All right, then.
-What about me?

250
00:20:15,214 --> 00:20:16,507
What should I do?

251
00:20:17,633 --> 00:20:18,759
You?

252
00:20:20,344 --> 00:20:21,679
You can...

253
00:20:22,263 --> 00:20:23,472
Uh...

254
00:20:24,515 --> 00:20:26,100
read some papers.

255
00:20:26,183 --> 00:20:27,351
What papers?

256
00:20:28,811 --> 00:20:31,188
Anything. Read broadly.

257
00:20:32,189 --> 00:20:34,191
You need to get up to speed
on current trends

258
00:20:34,734 --> 00:20:36,152
What trends?

259
00:20:37,403 --> 00:20:38,946
Whatever you find interesting.

260
00:20:40,865 --> 00:20:43,117
Read anything
that catches your eye. Anything.

261
00:21:26,744 --> 00:21:29,747
SEOHAN NATIONAL UNIVERSITY

262
00:21:34,585 --> 00:21:36,545
Here, I collected all the assignments.

263
00:21:37,087 --> 00:21:39,048
You didn't have
to carry something so heavy.

264
00:21:39,131 --> 00:21:40,341
-Give it to me.
-It's okay.

265
00:21:40,424 --> 00:21:42,510
-Where should I put it?
-You can put it here.

266
00:21:49,725 --> 00:21:51,852
I'm going to head out now.

267
00:21:52,436 --> 00:21:53,646
Huh?

268
00:21:53,729 --> 00:21:54,730
Ah!

269
00:21:54,814 --> 00:21:56,857
I'm done too, actually. Wait up.

270
00:21:58,567 --> 00:21:59,777
Let's head out together.

271
00:22:04,907 --> 00:22:06,242
Want to grab dinner together?

272
00:22:07,993 --> 00:22:09,495
Do you have any plans tonight?

273
00:22:11,288 --> 00:22:13,707
No, I don't.

274
00:22:15,209 --> 00:22:17,127
But I'm not hungry at all right now.

275
00:22:18,128 --> 00:22:19,129
Oh.

276
00:22:34,478 --> 00:22:35,855
So how was your first day?

277
00:22:37,022 --> 00:22:39,441
First days are always
a little hectic, right?

278
00:22:41,193 --> 00:22:43,863
Yeah, I guess.

279
00:22:47,199 --> 00:22:51,078
Read as many papers as you can
when you have time. It'll help you learn.

280
00:22:52,705 --> 00:22:53,706
Okay.

281
00:22:57,251 --> 00:22:58,711
You were hungry, weren't you?

282
00:23:00,796 --> 00:23:03,966
I'm not eating because I'm hungry.
I'm just eating.

283
00:23:05,467 --> 00:23:07,136
[muttering] That doesn't fool me.

284
00:23:08,512 --> 00:23:09,805
What are you laughing about?

285
00:23:10,848 --> 00:23:11,849
I didn't laugh.

286
00:23:13,642 --> 00:23:14,852
I don't want to eat anymore.

287
00:23:14,935 --> 00:23:16,478
Come on, why?

288
00:23:17,771 --> 00:23:19,815
All right, I'm sorry. Eat up. Please.

289
00:23:30,618 --> 00:23:31,619
I...

290
00:23:32,870 --> 00:23:34,580
don't have a sister.

291
00:23:36,165 --> 00:23:39,710
And it's not like
I have a lot of dating experience,

292
00:23:39,793 --> 00:23:41,045
so I'm kind of clueless.

293
00:23:46,133 --> 00:23:47,593
I was pretty drunk that day too.

294
00:23:49,845 --> 00:23:51,388
You know, that...

295
00:23:52,723 --> 00:23:53,724
That...

296
00:23:56,810 --> 00:23:58,270
That day...

297
00:24:00,105 --> 00:24:01,106
when you...

298
00:24:03,567 --> 00:24:05,819
That day? What do you mean by "that day"?

299
00:24:08,489 --> 00:24:09,490
That...

300
00:24:10,950 --> 00:24:14,912
Do you mean the day of my welcome party?

301
00:24:15,496 --> 00:24:16,497
Yes.

302
00:24:18,457 --> 00:24:20,292
Did I throw up on your clothes?

303
00:24:20,376 --> 00:24:21,377
Hmm?

304
00:24:22,378 --> 00:24:23,671
No, not that.

305
00:24:26,507 --> 00:24:30,094
Well, I remember I was singing.
No, actually...

306
00:24:30,761 --> 00:24:32,846
I remember getting into the taxi.

307
00:24:34,139 --> 00:24:36,058
But after that, I don't remember anything.

308
00:24:38,477 --> 00:24:41,397
You don't remember? Anything at all?

309
00:24:42,564 --> 00:24:45,985
Did I hit you
or curse at you or something?

310
00:24:46,860 --> 00:24:48,028
No.

311
00:24:48,112 --> 00:24:49,446
And I didn't throw up either?

312
00:24:49,530 --> 00:24:50,656
No, you didn't.

313
00:24:54,410 --> 00:24:56,704
[sighing] I don't remember what I did,

314
00:24:57,621 --> 00:25:01,417
but if I did something wrong,
I'm so sorry.

315
00:25:02,751 --> 00:25:05,212
I didn't mean to do it, I was just...

316
00:25:06,005 --> 00:25:07,715
I'm so sorry.

317
00:25:10,217 --> 00:25:13,012
It's okay. If you don't remember,
don't worry about it.

318
00:25:14,346 --> 00:25:16,015
I can't handle alcohol very well.

319
00:25:16,098 --> 00:25:19,018
Whenever I drink,
I always end up doing something stupid.

320
00:25:22,312 --> 00:25:23,313
I'm sorry.

321
00:25:23,897 --> 00:25:26,400
No. It was my bad.

322
00:25:27,234 --> 00:25:28,485
It's just... [sighs]

323
00:25:32,531 --> 00:25:33,532
Are you done eating?

324
00:25:35,284 --> 00:25:36,285
Yes.

325
00:25:36,368 --> 00:25:38,037
If you're done, should we head out?

326
00:25:53,802 --> 00:25:55,804
I'll walk you to the bus stop.

327
00:25:58,640 --> 00:26:02,394
By the way, when will I get my computer?

328
00:26:04,104 --> 00:26:06,231
That? You'll get it soon.

329
00:26:07,399 --> 00:26:08,650
When exactly is "soon"?

330
00:26:12,863 --> 00:26:15,574
They've shipped it,
so it should be here in a few days.

331
00:26:16,867 --> 00:26:20,579
How many days exactly?
Tomorrow? The day after?

332
00:26:21,580 --> 00:26:24,041
How am I supposed to know exactly?

333
00:26:26,043 --> 00:26:29,254
So you don't know when it'll get here.

334
00:26:30,506 --> 00:26:33,217
What am I supposed to do until then?
Just sit around?

335
00:26:34,676 --> 00:26:37,513
Well, like I said earlier,
you can read papers and study.

336
00:26:38,764 --> 00:26:41,141
I can read papers at home too.

337
00:26:41,225 --> 00:26:43,393
What's the point
of coming to the lab, then?

338
00:26:45,979 --> 00:26:46,980
Jeez.

339
00:26:48,941 --> 00:26:53,987
And if there's only one computer,
you should've given it to me first.

340
00:26:54,613 --> 00:26:57,658
Why did you give it to Kim Sejin?
He joined after me. I have seniority.

341
00:27:00,619 --> 00:27:01,620
Hey, you...

342
00:27:02,204 --> 00:27:04,331
You don't have seniority.

343
00:27:04,414 --> 00:27:06,667
You joined us just three days
before he did.

344
00:27:07,167 --> 00:27:09,670
I don't care if it was three days
or four days.

345
00:27:09,753 --> 00:27:12,339
You still should've given it
to me first, not him.

346
00:27:14,174 --> 00:27:15,968
Why do you think I gave it to him?

347
00:27:16,468 --> 00:27:19,179
You need MATLAB to run Simulink,

348
00:27:19,263 --> 00:27:21,515
and that computer
already has it installed.

349
00:27:21,598 --> 00:27:23,517
That's why I gave it to him.

350
00:27:24,309 --> 00:27:25,769
And frankly, you...

351
00:27:25,853 --> 00:27:29,189
Do you even know how to use MATLAB?
What about Simulink?

352
00:27:32,442 --> 00:27:33,610
If I don't know...

353
00:27:34,528 --> 00:27:37,155
Then you can teach me, right?

354
00:27:37,239 --> 00:27:40,033
Don't look down on me, and show me.
I'm a fast learner.

355
00:27:40,117 --> 00:27:42,369
When did I look down on you?

356
00:27:43,328 --> 00:27:44,496
What are you, a high schooler?

357
00:27:44,580 --> 00:27:46,164
-An undergrad?
-[sighs]

358
00:27:46,248 --> 00:27:49,418
Seriously, do I have
to teach you every little thing?

359
00:27:50,460 --> 00:27:53,630
You need to look things up
and study on your own. And I...

360
00:27:54,381 --> 00:27:57,467
I even told you to read papers.
But you called it sitting around.

361
00:27:58,427 --> 00:28:01,179
Fine. If reading papers
is just sitting around,

362
00:28:01,263 --> 00:28:02,848
go home and sit around.

363
00:28:02,931 --> 00:28:04,141
Don't come into the lab.

364
00:28:11,189 --> 00:28:12,816
Do you have anything else to say?

365
00:28:16,570 --> 00:28:20,490
I know you never liked me from the start.

366
00:28:22,117 --> 00:28:24,202
You didn't even want me to switch majors.

367
00:28:27,414 --> 00:28:29,291
I'll just take the subway home today.

368
00:28:34,796 --> 00:28:37,007
[muttering softly] God.
You've got to be kidding me.

369
00:31:15,916 --> 00:31:17,459
SEOHAN NATIONAL UNIVERSITY TEST PAPER
NAME KIM SEJIN

370
00:31:27,344 --> 00:31:30,263
SEOHAN NATIONAL UNIVERSITY TEST PAPER
NAME LIM YOUJIN

371
00:32:27,904 --> 00:32:29,364
All right, let's see.

372
00:32:44,671 --> 00:32:45,755
Let's see.

373
00:32:53,471 --> 00:32:54,472
Hello?

374
00:32:55,599 --> 00:32:58,768
You picked up fast.
Hey, I have something to ask you.

375
00:33:00,520 --> 00:33:04,107
What do you mean, birthday? Please.
Why don't you worry about your boyfriend?

376
00:33:06,735 --> 00:33:11,573
Anyway, that's not why I called.
That computer you used, what brand was it?

377
00:33:14,326 --> 00:33:19,289
Yeah. You know,
the one you used in the lab. That one.

378
00:33:32,552 --> 00:33:33,970
PARK MINJAE

379
00:33:34,054 --> 00:33:35,972
[Minjae] <i>You better show up</i>
<i>on time tomorrow.</i>

380
00:33:36,056 --> 00:33:38,934
<i>If you're late,</i>
<i>I'm going to send you to Dieland.</i>

381
00:34:57,554 --> 00:34:58,555
Hi.

382
00:35:01,558 --> 00:35:02,642
You aren't late.

383
00:35:03,643 --> 00:35:04,644
No.

384
00:35:07,480 --> 00:35:08,815
Did you have breakfast?

385
00:35:59,157 --> 00:36:00,992
Isn't that Lim Youjin?

386
00:36:02,202 --> 00:36:04,871
It's her, right? And next to her
is the research assistant.

387
00:36:05,872 --> 00:36:09,584
She just fits in wherever she goes.
She makes friends so easily too.

388
00:36:11,294 --> 00:36:12,420
It's nice to see.

389
00:36:14,130 --> 00:36:16,049
Do you happen to know him too?

390
00:36:18,968 --> 00:36:20,679
I don't really know him.

391
00:36:40,907 --> 00:36:43,493
Go on in. Come on.

392
00:36:53,503 --> 00:36:54,504
Oh!

393
00:36:55,004 --> 00:36:56,715
When did this get here?

394
00:36:57,841 --> 00:36:59,259
Well, I don't know.

395
00:37:00,301 --> 00:37:01,302
Oh.

396
00:37:01,386 --> 00:37:04,973
Was it delivered last night?
It must've been last night, after we left.

397
00:37:05,056 --> 00:37:08,226
I told you it'd be here soon.
I told you to just wait a little.

398
00:37:08,309 --> 00:37:10,562
Yeah, that was faster than I thought.

399
00:37:11,771 --> 00:37:13,398
Try turning it on. Here.

400
00:37:33,418 --> 00:37:35,378
Wow, it's so fast. [gasps]

401
00:37:37,380 --> 00:37:39,340
All the software's already set up, too.

402
00:37:40,884 --> 00:37:43,136
This is brand-new.
I got a brand-new computer.

403
00:37:43,219 --> 00:37:44,220
Yeah.

404
00:37:45,305 --> 00:37:46,389
Do you like it?

405
00:37:46,931 --> 00:37:49,017
Yeah. I absolutely love it.

406
00:37:50,268 --> 00:37:52,937
It's really expensive.

407
00:37:53,813 --> 00:37:57,650
Yeah, I can tell by just looking at it.
This is an expensive, latest model.

408
00:37:58,485 --> 00:38:00,069
So the rumor was true.

409
00:38:00,695 --> 00:38:02,322
Rumor? What rumor?

410
00:38:02,864 --> 00:38:06,743
I heard engineering schools have money
and get tons of corporate sponsorships.

411
00:38:06,826 --> 00:38:09,579
What? Engineering schools
don't have a lot of money.

412
00:38:10,121 --> 00:38:13,208
Maybe you don't, but our school does.

413
00:38:14,667 --> 00:38:17,337
[sighs] Thank you, school,
and whoever made this happen.

414
00:38:17,420 --> 00:38:18,963
I'll take good care of it.

415
00:38:24,969 --> 00:38:26,304
We got a new computer?

416
00:38:28,264 --> 00:38:30,183
Oh. When did you get it?

417
00:38:31,017 --> 00:38:32,268
It's the latest model.

418
00:38:32,352 --> 00:38:34,354
-Yeah.
-This thing is high-end!

419
00:38:35,271 --> 00:38:37,982
What GPU does it have?
I bet it's got a lot of storage too.

420
00:38:38,107 --> 00:38:39,108
Uh...

421
00:38:39,818 --> 00:38:42,403
[sighing grimly] My computer was so slow

422
00:38:42,487 --> 00:38:45,573
trying to run MATLAB, SolidWorks,
and RecurDyn all at once.

423
00:38:45,657 --> 00:38:47,325
-Yeah.
-This is perfect.

424
00:38:48,368 --> 00:38:49,369
Huh?

425
00:38:49,452 --> 00:38:50,453
I can...

426
00:38:52,247 --> 00:38:53,456
use this, right?

427
00:39:01,381 --> 00:39:05,510
I... can use this, right?

428
00:39:08,555 --> 00:39:09,556
This?

429
00:39:15,520 --> 00:39:18,648
Right, but then...

430
00:39:19,274 --> 00:39:21,150
Yeah, I mean, you...

431
00:39:22,735 --> 00:39:26,531
You'll probably get more use out of it.

432
00:39:28,032 --> 00:39:34,247
Then, Youjin, you take that one,
and Sejin, you take this one.

433
00:39:34,330 --> 00:39:35,331
Yes!

434
00:39:37,959 --> 00:39:39,127
What's wrong?

435
00:39:41,087 --> 00:39:42,088
What are you doing?

436
00:39:43,631 --> 00:39:45,842
I said, what are you doing?

437
00:39:46,551 --> 00:39:48,261
I can't take this anymore.

438
00:39:49,554 --> 00:39:51,973
Take what? You can just use any computer.

439
00:39:52,056 --> 00:39:53,391
-They're the same.
-Forget it.

440
00:39:53,474 --> 00:39:55,101
I don't need any of this anymore.

441
00:39:55,184 --> 00:39:57,353
I clearly don't have what it takes.
I'm useless.

442
00:39:57,437 --> 00:39:59,772
I was never qualified
to be here in the first place.

443
00:40:00,565 --> 00:40:02,984
Sticking around
when lack the qualifications or skills

444
00:40:03,067 --> 00:40:05,194
would only make things harder
for everyone.

445
00:40:06,279 --> 00:40:08,239
I just can't do this anymore.

446
00:40:09,198 --> 00:40:10,491
I'm leaving the lab.

447
00:40:11,326 --> 00:40:12,327
What?

448
00:40:12,827 --> 00:40:16,247
I stay up studying every night
and only get three, four hours of sleep.

449
00:40:16,873 --> 00:40:18,499
I'm reading papers and trying hard.

450
00:40:18,583 --> 00:40:22,420
But no matter how hard I try,
I just realize how much I don't know.

451
00:40:23,713 --> 00:40:26,883
No, it's more than that.
The amount I don't know keeps growing.

452
00:40:26,966 --> 00:40:29,510
The more I read,
the more I realize I don't know.

453
00:40:30,053 --> 00:40:33,765
So what am I supposed to do?
What more do you want from me?

454
00:40:37,435 --> 00:40:40,480
I already told you it was going to be hard

455
00:40:42,273 --> 00:40:44,776
and to think carefully
before you make a decision.

456
00:40:47,904 --> 00:40:48,905
Fine.

457
00:40:49,864 --> 00:40:51,282
I guess it's my fault again.

458
00:40:54,118 --> 00:40:55,662
Thanks for the lesson.

459
00:40:59,749 --> 00:41:00,750
All right.

460
00:41:01,918 --> 00:41:04,754
Bring me your withdrawal form
and a written explanation by tomorrow.

461
00:41:04,837 --> 00:41:06,005
I'll email them to you.

462
00:41:17,350 --> 00:41:18,601
What's going on?

463
00:41:18,685 --> 00:41:20,770
Minjae, did something happen?

464
00:41:32,365 --> 00:41:33,366
What's the matter?

465
00:41:34,283 --> 00:41:35,410
Did something happen?

466
00:41:35,910 --> 00:41:36,995
I'm not sure.

467
00:43:02,663 --> 00:43:07,168
SEOHAN NATIONAL UNIVERSITY TEST PAPER
NAME LIM YOUJIN

468
00:43:07,251 --> 00:43:11,631
SEOHAN NATIONAL UNIVERSITY TEST PAPER
NAME KIM SEJIN

469
00:43:12,215 --> 00:43:15,384
Come on, you did a pretty good job.
Why are you crying?

470
00:43:16,094 --> 00:43:18,679
[crying] What do you mean, pretty good?
It's a mess.

471
00:43:23,434 --> 00:43:27,980
I made the question too hard. Yeah, I...

472
00:43:28,064 --> 00:43:32,026
What about Kim Sejin?
How did Kim Sejin do so well?

473
00:43:32,985 --> 00:43:34,487
Is he a genius?

474
00:43:34,570 --> 00:43:36,572
Is he a genius and I'm just stupid?

475
00:43:37,073 --> 00:43:41,369
Hey, He's him and you're you.
Why compare yourself to him?

476
00:43:41,452 --> 00:43:44,705
I'm not comparing myself to him.
I'm just so stupid.

477
00:43:45,957 --> 00:43:47,792
Maybe you're a genius.

478
00:43:48,501 --> 00:43:50,253
Are you making fun of me right now?

479
00:43:53,506 --> 00:43:55,675
At the beginning of the movie
<i>Good Will Hunting,</i>

480
00:43:56,342 --> 00:43:59,345
Matt Damon's character
works as a janitor at MIT. But then--

481
00:43:59,428 --> 00:44:01,639
I told you I haven't seen that movie.

482
00:44:01,722 --> 00:44:03,641
Kim Sejin has, but I haven't.

483
00:44:03,724 --> 00:44:07,728
So go talk about that movie
with Kim Sejin and leave me alone.

484
00:44:09,480 --> 00:44:11,566
Why did you even let me in?

485
00:44:12,108 --> 00:44:15,403
I haven't seen the movie,
I can't do math, and I'm so stupid.

486
00:44:18,406 --> 00:44:21,826
[sniffles] Forget it.
Let's just stop here.

487
00:44:23,035 --> 00:44:26,205
I don't want to keep going on and on
like this either.

488
00:44:29,125 --> 00:44:32,837
I'm so sorry for causing you
so much trouble all this time.

489
00:44:34,714 --> 00:44:39,719
I may be leaving,
but I'll keep rooting for you from afar.

490
00:44:41,053 --> 00:44:43,639
No. Hey, wait. Okay, fine.

491
00:44:43,723 --> 00:44:46,475
Okay, sit down for a second.
Hey, just for a second.

492
00:44:53,900 --> 00:44:55,526
Then, have you seen <i>Harry Potter?</i>

493
00:44:58,029 --> 00:45:01,073
Come on, you've seen that one, right?

494
00:45:02,325 --> 00:45:04,535
In <i>Harry Potter,</i> there's this talking hat.

495
00:45:04,619 --> 00:45:07,997
When Harry Potter puts it on,
it tells him,

496
00:45:08,080 --> 00:45:12,793
"You're a Gryffindor.
You're a Gryffindor."

497
00:45:14,503 --> 00:45:16,047
We have one at our school too.

498
00:45:17,465 --> 00:45:18,758
A talking hat.

499
00:45:19,967 --> 00:45:21,135
Want to meet it?

500
00:45:26,140 --> 00:45:27,475
Okay. Come this way.

501
00:45:31,395 --> 00:45:32,396
Oh?

502
00:45:34,106 --> 00:45:35,691
I guess he hasn't come in yet.

503
00:45:40,696 --> 00:45:42,240
Oh!

504
00:45:42,323 --> 00:45:44,992
-Good morning, Professor.
-Hi.

505
00:45:45,076 --> 00:45:46,953
Do you have a minute?

506
00:45:48,162 --> 00:45:49,413
Sure. Yeah, come in.

507
00:45:59,006 --> 00:46:00,716
[whispering] Is he the talking hat?

508
00:46:02,009 --> 00:46:03,511
[whispering] Yeah, he is.

509
00:46:11,686 --> 00:46:14,480
Sorry, my assistant is not here yet.
Is this okay?

510
00:46:14,563 --> 00:46:16,899
-Yes, it's okay. Thank you.
-Please, sit down.

511
00:46:16,983 --> 00:46:17,984
Thank you.

512
00:46:19,110 --> 00:46:20,778
So you want me to look at something?

513
00:46:21,279 --> 00:46:23,447
Right. It's just this...

514
00:46:26,033 --> 00:46:27,034
Here.

515
00:46:30,913 --> 00:46:31,914
Didn't...

516
00:46:33,374 --> 00:46:34,667
I look at this the other day?

517
00:46:34,750 --> 00:46:37,253
Yes, that's right.
You looked it over last time

518
00:46:37,336 --> 00:46:40,214
and said it showed signs of genius.

519
00:46:40,298 --> 00:46:41,299
I did?

520
00:46:41,382 --> 00:46:42,383
Yes.

521
00:46:45,303 --> 00:46:47,847
I said I saw potential,
not signs of genius.

522
00:46:50,683 --> 00:46:51,684
Ah.

523
00:46:51,767 --> 00:46:53,978
Is she the one who's
from a different department?

524
00:46:54,061 --> 00:46:55,855
Yes, that's right. It's her.

525
00:46:58,816 --> 00:47:00,568
Have we met before?

526
00:47:01,152 --> 00:47:02,153
Sorry?

527
00:47:02,945 --> 00:47:04,405
I feel like we've met somewhere.

528
00:47:06,907 --> 00:47:09,160
I don't think we've met.

529
00:47:10,411 --> 00:47:11,412
Okay.

530
00:47:13,247 --> 00:47:16,542
Last time, you said she had talent--

531
00:47:16,625 --> 00:47:17,626
Yeah.

532
00:47:21,547 --> 00:47:22,798
Let me ask you one thing.

533
00:47:23,466 --> 00:47:26,052
This is a basic question.

534
00:47:27,053 --> 00:47:28,679
Why does one plus one equal two?

535
00:47:30,765 --> 00:47:32,141
[Minjae] Mmm...

536
00:47:33,684 --> 00:47:35,561
Because it conventionally represents--

537
00:47:35,644 --> 00:47:37,897
So why was the numeral 2
chosen to represent it?

538
00:47:40,608 --> 00:47:42,568
Because it looks pretty?

539
00:47:43,986 --> 00:47:45,696
See? She thinks differently.

540
00:47:46,280 --> 00:47:47,281
Oh.

541
00:47:49,742 --> 00:47:51,243
Don't you think it's pretty?

542
00:47:51,327 --> 00:47:53,996
I think about that a lot
when I'm solving math problems.

543
00:47:54,789 --> 00:47:57,541
You know, the harmony,
the way things change...

544
00:47:57,625 --> 00:48:00,711
Sometimes it feels
like a dance, or even a song.

545
00:48:01,128 --> 00:48:02,296
Hmm.

546
00:48:03,047 --> 00:48:04,173
Hmm.

547
00:48:04,256 --> 00:48:05,341
That's romantic.

548
00:48:06,258 --> 00:48:07,259
Pardon?

549
00:48:07,343 --> 00:48:13,682
Yeah, I think I heard somewhere
that math is the language of God.

550
00:48:13,766 --> 00:48:15,851
Right. That's romantic too.

551
00:48:16,477 --> 00:48:19,688
That it's the language of God
translated into human language.

552
00:48:19,772 --> 00:48:20,773
-Right.
-Yeah.

553
00:48:23,609 --> 00:48:26,904
If numbers are God's language,

554
00:48:27,530 --> 00:48:31,534
then this answer
is God being pretty chatty.

555
00:48:32,284 --> 00:48:36,956
But when you're learning a new language,
being chatty is actually a huge advantage.

556
00:48:40,501 --> 00:48:42,294
I wouldn't call it genius,

557
00:48:43,963 --> 00:48:46,590
but I do see talent and potential.

558
00:48:47,091 --> 00:48:48,092
That's how I'd put it.

559
00:48:51,971 --> 00:48:54,265
Are you interested
in continuing your studies?

560
00:48:55,224 --> 00:48:56,225
Uh...

561
00:48:57,601 --> 00:48:58,686
Hmm...

562
00:48:59,311 --> 00:49:00,438
Mmm.

563
00:49:00,521 --> 00:49:02,982
Well, think about it.

564
00:49:03,816 --> 00:49:05,443
Okay, I'll think about it.

565
00:49:16,287 --> 00:49:19,498
That professor is a bit strange, isn't he?

566
00:49:22,001 --> 00:49:23,002
Yeah.

567
00:49:24,545 --> 00:49:26,922
Everyone says he's a genius, though.

568
00:49:29,550 --> 00:49:33,012
A lot of geniuses are weird, though.
They're kind of nuts.

569
00:49:33,846 --> 00:49:37,850
Then you must
be a super, super, super genius.

570
00:49:43,606 --> 00:49:47,860
Anyway, I knew I had talent.
It just hasn't blossomed yet.

571
00:49:49,069 --> 00:49:50,613
I'm not like Kim Sejin.

572
00:49:51,363 --> 00:49:55,326
I'm a genius, and he's just a smart man.

573
00:49:58,913 --> 00:50:01,957
Then will you let him use the computer?

574
00:50:03,000 --> 00:50:05,336
Not just the computer.
He can use whatever he wants.

575
00:50:06,045 --> 00:50:08,547
Now, I'm someone
who speaks the language of God.

576
00:50:10,341 --> 00:50:13,302
Which means I'm a goddess.
A genius goddess.

577
00:50:16,597 --> 00:50:19,141
You're really... You're really cute.

578
00:50:26,607 --> 00:50:28,192
-Let's go.
-Okay.

579
00:50:30,861 --> 00:50:32,196
Done with that? I'll take it.

580
00:50:32,988 --> 00:50:33,989
Thank you.

581
00:50:39,995 --> 00:50:43,207
[Seohyun] I'm asking why you were
using Minjae's computer.

582
00:50:43,290 --> 00:50:44,875
I gave it to him for his birthday.

583
00:50:45,668 --> 00:50:47,253
-I thought it was school--
-Louder.

584
00:50:47,336 --> 00:50:48,337
-Hey!
-You thought it--

585
00:50:48,420 --> 00:50:49,880
What the... When did you get here?

586
00:50:49,964 --> 00:50:51,590
What? I just got here. Why?

587
00:50:52,216 --> 00:50:54,051
Didn't you go to work today?

588
00:50:54,134 --> 00:50:55,469
I took the afternoon off.

589
00:50:55,553 --> 00:50:58,722
Hey, will you please
keep the kids in line?

590
00:50:58,806 --> 00:51:01,100
There's no discipline around here.
Absolutely none.

591
00:51:02,851 --> 00:51:05,437
I got busy at work
and stopped checking in for a while,

592
00:51:05,521 --> 00:51:08,274
and this is what happens to the lab?

593
00:51:08,857 --> 00:51:11,318
Nobody even knew it's your birthday today.

594
00:51:11,402 --> 00:51:12,486
-Hey.
-Well...

595
00:51:12,570 --> 00:51:15,864
Minjae goes by the lunar calendar
for his birthday, and I got mixed up.

596
00:51:15,948 --> 00:51:18,367
If you got them mixed up,
just celebrate both!

597
00:51:18,951 --> 00:51:20,160
How hard is that?

598
00:51:20,703 --> 00:51:22,037
No, it's not hard.

599
00:51:23,455 --> 00:51:26,875
You've gotten way too comfortable.
You have no respect for Minjae, do you?

600
00:51:26,959 --> 00:51:28,127
[all] No.

601
00:51:28,669 --> 00:51:30,087
[yells] Everybody, out!

602
00:51:30,588 --> 00:51:31,589
What are you doing?

603
00:51:33,007 --> 00:51:34,592
Too slow!

604
00:51:38,887 --> 00:51:40,055
Aren't you going to go?

605
00:51:40,681 --> 00:51:41,682
Me too?

606
00:51:41,765 --> 00:51:44,143
Of course. Do you think
you're an exception?

607
00:51:45,019 --> 00:51:46,145
-No.
-Uh...

608
00:51:49,773 --> 00:51:51,525
What? What is it?

609
00:52:12,880 --> 00:52:15,507
[whispering] Where are we going now?

610
00:52:16,258 --> 00:52:18,802
[whispering] We're driving to Dieland.

611
00:52:20,054 --> 00:52:23,974
Wait, Dieland is real? It actually exists?

612
00:52:26,769 --> 00:52:29,021
[whispering] By the way, why is she
in a school uniform?

613
00:52:31,523 --> 00:52:35,861
Most engineering students are nuts.

614
00:52:39,406 --> 00:52:41,533
[whispering] It's not
about being engineering students.

615
00:52:41,617 --> 00:52:44,036
I think
it's a Seohan National University thing.

616
00:52:44,119 --> 00:52:46,622
KAIST wasn't like this.
Everyone there was normal.

617
00:52:46,705 --> 00:52:50,000
Jeez, you're wearing a school uniform.
You've got to be kidding me.

618
00:52:50,501 --> 00:52:53,462
What? This is what you're supposed
to wear to a birthday party.

619
00:52:54,630 --> 00:52:56,298
I told you to wear yours too.

620
00:52:57,508 --> 00:52:59,259
Hey, that still fits you?

621
00:53:00,344 --> 00:53:03,430
I know, right? I'm still fit.
I can totally pull it off.

622
00:53:03,514 --> 00:53:05,683
I've gained weight,
so mine doesn't fit anymore.

623
00:53:06,600 --> 00:53:07,810
Let's get you a new one.

624
00:53:08,477 --> 00:53:09,478
No.

625
00:53:10,229 --> 00:53:12,481
Then we can match every year
on your birthday.

626
00:53:12,564 --> 00:53:13,691
I don't need it.

627
00:53:14,233 --> 00:53:16,402
-Should I get you one?
-I said, I don't need it.

628
00:53:16,485 --> 00:53:17,611
Why not?

629
00:53:17,695 --> 00:53:19,405
-I'll buy a new one.
-I don't want it.

630
00:53:19,488 --> 00:53:21,657
I'm never going to wear it. No way.

631
00:53:37,297 --> 00:53:40,843
I haven't been here in ages.
But why is this place called Dieland?

632
00:54:43,280 --> 00:54:44,656
[Sejin] I didn't realize it before,

633
00:54:46,074 --> 00:54:48,035
but are those two a couple?

634
00:54:49,369 --> 00:54:52,623
She got him an expensive computer
for his birthday,

635
00:54:53,165 --> 00:54:54,541
and they seem really close.

636
00:54:55,083 --> 00:54:57,753
They're not a couple,
but they're high school sweethearts.

637
00:54:57,836 --> 00:55:01,590
No. It wasn't mutual, it was a crush.

638
00:55:02,424 --> 00:55:04,051
It was just a one-sided crush.

639
00:55:06,553 --> 00:55:10,766
Who had a crush on who?
Did Seohyun have a crush on Minjae?

640
00:55:10,849 --> 00:55:13,435
No, it's not like that.

641
00:55:15,312 --> 00:55:19,107
In high school,
Seohyun was the top student

642
00:55:19,191 --> 00:55:23,487
and the most popular girl in the school,
while Minjae was dead last.

643
00:55:23,570 --> 00:55:28,450
But he studied really hard
to get into the same university as her.

644
00:55:28,534 --> 00:55:30,035
That's how he got into our school

645
00:55:30,118 --> 00:55:32,371
and even followed her
into mechanical engineering.

646
00:55:33,539 --> 00:55:35,499
[Chansoo] It's straight out
of a coming-of-age manga.

647
00:55:36,208 --> 00:55:38,168
And a high school romance.

648
00:55:38,877 --> 00:55:42,339
It's kind of like<i> Slam Dunk.</i>
Haruko Akagi and Hanamichi Sakuragi.

649
00:55:43,465 --> 00:55:46,051
But they never dated? Why not?

650
00:55:46,134 --> 00:55:49,846
Because Seohyun was super popular,
while Minjae was the kind of guy

651
00:55:49,930 --> 00:55:53,267
who second-guessed everything
and made things way too complicated.

652
00:55:54,768 --> 00:55:56,103
That's why they never got together.

653
00:55:58,939 --> 00:56:00,566
Well, maybe that's not the reason.

654
00:56:02,859 --> 00:56:04,486
Maybe it was because of his leg.

655
00:56:07,698 --> 00:56:09,074
-Just try it on once.
-No.

656
00:56:09,157 --> 00:56:10,242
Please.

657
00:56:10,325 --> 00:56:12,119
-Damn it.
-Here. Just take this.

658
00:56:12,202 --> 00:56:13,912
Hey, guys, take one each. [grunts]

659
00:56:18,375 --> 00:56:20,085
Seohyun, when are we going home?

660
00:56:20,168 --> 00:56:23,463
We should stay for the parade
and the fireworks. That's the highlight.

661
00:56:23,547 --> 00:56:27,134
Wait, then we'll have
to stay here past eight.

662
00:56:29,136 --> 00:56:30,512
Your expressions...

663
00:56:30,596 --> 00:56:32,514
Look at you, Taeho, all grown up, huh?

664
00:56:32,598 --> 00:56:34,516
No, we're good. We don't need to see that.

665
00:56:34,600 --> 00:56:36,184
We're not kids. Come on, let's go.

666
00:56:36,268 --> 00:56:37,811
[Seohyun] Come on, that's the best part.

667
00:56:37,894 --> 00:56:40,105
-[Minjae] No, it's not.
-[Seohyun] Come on, let's watch it.

668
00:57:06,173 --> 00:57:07,841
I read <i>Slam Dunk.</i>

669
00:57:09,384 --> 00:57:10,552
You read it?

670
00:57:13,597 --> 00:57:17,768
Hanamichi Sakuragi was bad at basketball,
but he finds out Haruko likes it

671
00:57:17,851 --> 00:57:19,436
and he joins the basketball team.

672
00:57:19,519 --> 00:57:21,897
-That's basically it, right?
-Yeah, you read it.

673
00:57:22,481 --> 00:57:23,482
It's fun, isn't it?

674
00:57:24,775 --> 00:57:26,068
Not to me.

675
00:57:27,069 --> 00:57:30,197
I guess you like stories like that?
Because you relate to it so much?

676
00:57:31,198 --> 00:57:32,199
What?

677
00:57:35,285 --> 00:57:38,413
Sorry. I'm in a bit of a mood today.

678
00:57:40,624 --> 00:57:41,750
Why are you in a mood?

679
00:57:43,794 --> 00:57:45,379
I don't want to tell you why.

680
00:57:46,254 --> 00:57:49,132
It sounds childish
and unreasonable, even to me.

681
00:57:52,636 --> 00:57:53,637
Unless...

682
00:57:58,183 --> 00:58:01,228
If you put this on
and take a selfie with me,

683
00:58:01,311 --> 00:58:02,521
I think I'd feel better.

684
00:58:03,146 --> 00:58:04,147
No.

685
00:58:06,233 --> 00:58:08,193
Please, just one picture with it on.

686
00:58:08,276 --> 00:58:10,278
Why are you doing this?
No, I don't want to.

687
00:58:10,862 --> 00:58:12,948
-Please, just once.
-No.

688
00:58:13,031 --> 00:58:14,616
Not even once?

689
00:58:14,700 --> 00:58:18,704
Of course not. Why would you put that
on your head? I don't get it. No.

690
00:58:19,663 --> 00:58:20,997
I won't wait long.

691
00:58:22,541 --> 00:58:23,625
Five.

692
00:58:25,335 --> 00:58:26,336
Four.

693
00:58:27,879 --> 00:58:28,880
Three.

694
00:58:30,173 --> 00:58:31,174
Two.

695
00:58:33,510 --> 00:58:34,511
One.

696
00:58:43,520 --> 00:58:46,606
But no pictures, okay?
I'll put it on, and that's it.

697
01:00:20,617 --> 01:00:22,369
Are you looking for anything specific?

698
01:00:24,412 --> 01:00:25,413
No.

699
01:00:33,839 --> 01:00:35,549
Would you like to take a closer look?

700
01:00:36,800 --> 01:00:38,218
No, I'm okay.

701
01:00:41,805 --> 01:00:45,517
Then could you show me this one?

702
01:00:45,600 --> 01:00:46,601
Sure.

703
01:00:53,400 --> 01:00:57,946
INCOMING CALL
SUBIN

704
01:01:32,606 --> 01:01:34,441
It's been ages, hasn't it?

705
01:01:34,941 --> 01:01:36,151
Yeah.

706
01:01:36,234 --> 01:01:37,819
How have you been?

707
01:01:40,071 --> 01:01:43,199
It must be so hectic studying
and working as a TA at the same time.

708
01:01:46,244 --> 01:01:47,829
I'm sorry. It's all because of me.

709
01:01:48,330 --> 01:01:49,331
Hmm?

710
01:01:51,499 --> 01:01:52,834
It's not because of you.

711
01:01:54,002 --> 01:01:56,546
I was never good at making clothes anyway.

712
01:01:57,339 --> 01:02:00,800
And I wasn't sure about joining
Professor Kang's lab. You know that.

713
01:02:02,469 --> 01:02:05,972
Actually, I saw you on campus a few times.

714
01:02:07,015 --> 01:02:10,393
But I couldn't bring myself to say hi
or act like I knew you.

715
01:02:13,855 --> 01:02:16,983
Well, that's...
I know how small this field is.

716
01:02:18,902 --> 01:02:20,528
And you're still in the program.

717
01:02:21,112 --> 01:02:23,406
You have to study and get your degree,

718
01:02:23,490 --> 01:02:26,451
so, of course, you've got to stay
on Professor Kang's good side.

719
01:02:28,495 --> 01:02:31,331
I'm the one who talked back to her
and caused all that trouble.

720
01:02:31,957 --> 01:02:33,333
I was the one in the wrong.

721
01:02:34,751 --> 01:02:39,130
Actually, Professor Kang
has cooled off quite a bit.

722
01:02:41,299 --> 01:02:45,679
She said if you apologized,
she'd forgive you and accept it.

723
01:02:49,057 --> 01:02:50,642
She'd forgive me and accept it?

724
01:02:53,103 --> 01:02:55,438
Forgive me for what and accept what?

725
01:02:55,939 --> 01:02:59,275
Well, maybe "forgive"
isn't exactly the right word.

726
01:03:02,654 --> 01:03:05,407
But what good does it do
to get on the professor's bad side?

727
01:03:10,370 --> 01:03:12,414
Okay, I'll think about it.

728
01:03:12,497 --> 01:03:13,581
Really?

729
01:03:13,665 --> 01:03:14,666
Yeah.

730
01:03:18,712 --> 01:03:21,214
So, how's mechanical engineering?
Are you enjoying it?

731
01:03:22,424 --> 01:03:23,717
Yeah, it's fun.

732
01:03:24,676 --> 01:03:27,387
The lab assistant
is that guy from before, right?

733
01:03:29,222 --> 01:03:32,392
I honestly had no idea he was disabled.

734
01:03:33,476 --> 01:03:35,562
There was nothing unusual
about the way he walked, right?

735
01:03:37,313 --> 01:03:39,315
He doesn't limp or anything.

736
01:05:39,602 --> 01:05:42,188
What brings you in on a day off?

737
01:05:43,439 --> 01:05:45,441
Well, you're here on our day off too.

738
01:05:45,984 --> 01:05:47,152
Well, I'm just...

739
01:05:54,159 --> 01:05:55,160
What is it?

740
01:05:57,287 --> 01:06:00,582
It's your birthday present.
I promised I'd get you one.

741
01:06:00,665 --> 01:06:04,335
My birthday was ages ago. It's fine.

742
01:06:06,671 --> 01:06:10,091
There's the computer... No, not just that.

743
01:06:11,634 --> 01:06:13,845
I know you've been kind to me
in many other ways.

744
01:06:15,263 --> 01:06:17,307
I can't always be the one receiving.

745
01:06:17,891 --> 01:06:20,643
So you got me these? Do you know my size?

746
01:06:21,644 --> 01:06:23,021
I just took a guess.

747
01:06:23,646 --> 01:06:26,024
Try them on.
We can exchange them if they don't fit.

748
01:06:28,359 --> 01:06:31,237
Sure, it's a gift. I should try them on.

749
01:06:44,334 --> 01:06:45,335
Cute.

750
01:07:06,981 --> 01:07:07,982
Thanks.

751
01:07:28,378 --> 01:07:30,338
How are they? Do they fit?

752
01:07:30,880 --> 01:07:33,800
Yeah, they fit perfectly.
They're perfect. They're nice.

753
01:07:35,802 --> 01:07:38,680
Walk around in them.
You won't know until you try.

754
01:07:38,763 --> 01:07:40,139
Right. Okay.

755
01:07:42,058 --> 01:07:44,978
I don't think I've ever
worn this color before.

756
01:09:03,681 --> 01:09:07,602
BETWEEN STEPS

757
01:09:07,685 --> 01:09:09,187
What are those sneakers?

758
01:09:09,270 --> 01:09:10,605
Youjin gave them to me.

759
01:09:11,105 --> 01:09:13,232
[Taeho] <i>She was squishing</i>
<i>your face like this.</i>

760
01:09:13,316 --> 01:09:14,942
She had this mature, older vibe.

761
01:09:15,026 --> 01:09:16,778
She's someone I used to like.

762
01:09:16,861 --> 01:09:18,404
Shouldn't we do something?

763
01:09:18,488 --> 01:09:21,783
Just leave him be.
Let him live, die, or stay like garbage.

764
01:09:22,283 --> 01:09:26,162
I just couldn't believe it at the time,
so I wanted to see it for myself.

765
01:09:27,789 --> 01:09:33,419
[Minjae] <i>Imagine how I felt</i>
<i>after you left like that.</i>
